## Model choices I used in the notebook

I selected **Logistic Regression** as the main ML baseline because it is usually a strong TF-IDF baseline for multiclass text classification and is much more reliable than Random Forest on sparse text data. The notebook still includes optional cells for Naive Bayes and Random Forest so you can add extra comparisons.

For the TF-IDF deep neural network, I used **TruncatedSVD before the dense network** so the input becomes practical for a multi-layer DNN while still respecting the “TF-IDF + DNN” requirement.

For skip-gram, I used **gensim Word2Vec with `sg=1`**, trained on your own training corpus, which keeps the setup course-aligned and self-contained.

